  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The population of a country is doubling every 30 years and was 3 000 000 at the last census.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show, by establishing a pattern, why the population $P$ after $n$ years is $P=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{\\frac{n}{30}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p31-q8-a-short-pattern-0",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n=0:\\ P=3{,}000{,}000\\times2^0",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p31-q8-a-short-pattern-30",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n=30:\\ P=3{,}000{,}000\\times2^1",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p31-q8-a-short-pattern-60",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n=60:\\ P=3{,}000{,}000\\times2^2",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p31-q8-a-short-generalisation",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\therefore P=3{,}000{,}000\\times2^{\\frac{n}{30}}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}n&=0: &P&=3{,}000{,}000\\times2^0\\\\n&=30: &P&=3{,}000{,}000\\times2^1\\\\n&=60: &P&=3{,}000{,}000\\times2^2\\end{align*}$$\nThere are $\\frac{n}{30}$ doubling periods in $n$ years after the last census.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\therefore P&=3{,}000{,}000\\times2^{\\frac{n}{30}}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find when the population will be 1 billion, to 1 d.p.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "251.4 years\n\nSubstitute the target mass, isolate the exponential factor, then use logarithms to find the time.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P&=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{\\frac{n}{30}}\\\\1\\,000\\,000\\,000&=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{\\frac{n}{30}}\\\\\\frac{1000}{3}&=2^{\\frac{n}{30}}\\\\\\log_2\\left(\\frac{1000}{3}\\right)&=\\frac{n}{30}\\\\n&=30\\log_2\\left(\\frac{1000}{3}\\right)\\\\n&\\approx251.4\\text{ years}\\end{align*}$$\nThe population will be 1 billion 251.4 years after the last census.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      }
    ]
  },
